---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="ੴ Sri Guru Granth Sahib Ji — Raag Clock (traditional timing)" heading="Raag Clock">
  <section id="v-clock">
    <p class="clock-sub">
      When each raag is traditionally sung — shown as <b>attributed scholarly claims</b>, not facts.
      Where traditions disagree, both placements are kept with their sources.
      <a href="/divergence">See every disagreement →</a>
    </p>

    <!-- "What raag is it now?" -->
    <div class="card nowcard" id="nowCard">
      <div class="now-head">
        <h2 id="nowTitle">What raag is it now?</h2>
        <div class="mode-tgl" role="radiogroup" aria-label="How the watches are measured" id="modeTgl">
          <button type="button" role="radio" aria-checked="true" data-mode="fixed"
                  title="Eight fixed 3-hour watches, the first at 6 AM">Fixed</button>
          <button type="button" role="radio" aria-checked="false" data-mode="solar"
                  title="Four watches of daylight and four of night, from sunrise and sunset where you are">Solar</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div id="nowBody" aria-live="polite"><div class="hint">Loading the timing claims…</div></div>
      <div id="nowNext" class="now-next"></div>
      <div id="solarBox" class="solar-box" hidden></div>
    </div>

    <!-- the face, and the claims of the watch that was chosen -->
    <div class="card clockcard">
      <div class="clock-stage">
        <div class="clock-col">
          <div id="clockWrap" class="clock-dial"
               role="group" aria-label="Raag clock on your own 12-hour clock face: the ring shows the half of the day the hour hand is in. Each watch is a button; all eight are listed below."></div>
          <p id="clockReadout" class="clock-readout"></p>
        </div>
        <aside id="clockDetail" class="clock-detail" aria-live="polite" aria-label="The chosen watch"></aside>
      </div>
      <div class="clock-legend" id="clockLegend">
        <span><i class="lg lg-now"></i> the watch now</span>
        <span><i class="lg lg-day"></i> day watches (1–4)</span>
        <span><i class="lg lg-night"></i> night watches (5–8)</span>
        <span><i class="lg lg-bead"></i> a raag</span>
        <span><i class="lg lg-variant"></i> a disputed variant</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- the same content as lists: the full path for a keyboard and a screen reader -->
    <div class="card">
      <h2 class="clock-h">The eight watches</h2>
      <div id="watchList" class="watches"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card" id="seasonSec">
      <h2 class="clock-h">In season · any time</h2>
      <div id="seasonList" class="seasons"></div>
    </div>

    <!-- every claim: filter + search + a strip of the day per raag -->
    <div class="card explorer">
      <div class="exp-head">
        <div>
          <h2 class="clock-h">All timing claims</h2>
          <p class="exp-hint">Search and filter every attributed claim. The strip shows when each raag sounds across the day.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div id="claimsExplorer"></div>
    </div>

    <p class="clock-foot">Pahars were traditionally <b>solar</b>: four equal watches of daylight and four of
      night, so they stretch and shrink with the season. The fixed view places the first watch at 6 AM as a
      modern rendering; solar mode works out sunrise and sunset on this device (NOAA equations), and your
      location never leaves it. The dial is your own 12-hour clock: the ring shows the half of the day the
      hour hand is in (AM or PM), and each watch sits where the hand points at that time. Every placement here is an attributed claim with its citation.</p>
  </section>
  <script>import '../scripts/raagclock';</script>
</Base>
